{
  "$comment": [
    "JiggerJot's curated ingredient catalog, and the map from what two books call things to what",
    "they are. Built by seed/build_ingredients.py, which refuses to emit anything while a single raw",
    "name is unaccounted for.",
    "",
    "Ingredients are generic, not brands (JJ-017) - 'Bacardi Rum' is white rum and 'Smirnoff Vodka'",
    "is vodka. The exception is the ingredient that IS a product: nothing generic substitutes for",
    "Chartreuse in a Last Word, and 'herbal liqueur' would make the recipe unmakeable and the",
    "inventory meaningless. Those keep their proper names (JJ-033).",
    "",
    "'aliases' are what the books say. Case, surrounding whitespace, 'fresh'/'freshly squeezed',",
    "parentheticals and leading counts are stripped before matching, so only genuinely different",
    "words need listing here."
  ],
